Decision 222, CODEGEN.md §5.6, §5.8: no generator writes a dependent branch into a load.defines table (its As<Branch>Value), so the dependent type is refused, used or not, for gen/go (data here) as for gen/cpp; a field that refs the table is written.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local let kinds = load.defines("@features/a/kinds.h")

/// A switch.
type P(on: Bool) = match on { false => ref kinds, true => String }

/// A rule.
record Rule {
  /// Its kind.
  kind: ref kinds
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: data }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:6:6
  emit go in data mode cannot generate a dependent type

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
